tion. reduced-motion preferences always keep it still. offline & installation after the offline cache is ready, published pages and saved discussion snapshots can be read without a connection. posting and contribution links still need github. use install in the command menu where supported. otherwise, use your browser’s install menu, or share → add to home screen on iphone and ipad.      "} {:path "/search/", :title "Search the site", :description "Search the site", :type "page", :text "search the site search the site across every published buffer search the site a command, an idea, a person. open site search interactive search needs javascript. you can browse all indexed content below, or use your browser’s find command.       "} {:path "/snippets/eglot/", :title "Let Eglot do the introductions", :description "Connect a project to an installed language server.", :type "snippet", :text "let eglot do the introductions connect a project to an installed language server. snippet let eglot do the introductions  connect a project to an installed language server.     by   henrik kjerringvåg  built-in / development / eglot / language-server eglot is built into emacs 29 and later. you still need to install a language server for your language, such as clangd for c and c++. open a source file and run m-x eglot. emacs offers completion, diagnostics, and navigation using its ordinary editing commands. start interactively before adding the use-package declaration. that makes missing executables and project configuration problems easier to understand. the example starts eglot in c and c++ buffers; adapt the hooks for your language. completion, project navigation, flymake diagnostics, and eldoc documentation use familiar built-in interfaces rather than a separate dashboard.  ;; emacs 29+, with clangd installed separately.\n(use-package eglot\n  :ensure nil\n  :hook ((c-mode . eglot-ensure)\n         (c++-mode . eglot-ensure)))  read the documentation     hkjels   eglot ;; emacs 29+